# Agent collaboration (Dose)

Personal Next.js notes app. Keep GitHub writes conservative.

## Default posture

- **Read freely**: code, docs, git history, GitHub (read), web.
- **Write locally** when the user asked for the work (features, fixes, plans, rules).
- **Commit** when the user asks, or when they said commits as you go in this session.
- **Do not push or open PRs** unless the user clearly asks in this conversation.

## Requires explicit approval each time

| Action | Examples |
|--------|----------|
| Git push | `git push`, `-u origin`, force-push |
| Pull requests | create, edit, merge, close |
| PR comments | review comments on GitHub |

Prepare locally (branch, commit, PR body draft) and ask before publishing.

## No Cursor attribution

Never add `Co-authored-by: Cursor` or `Made with Cursor`. Before push/`gh pr create`, confirm `~/.cursor/cli-config.json` has both attribution flags `false`.

## After local work

Report: (1) what changed, (2) tests/lint/build, (3) suggested next step — e.g. "Say push when ready".
